cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  gonzalgo: provenance auditing for machine-checked mathematics
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gonzalez
    given-names: Vince
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3640-014X'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/zengineco/gonzalgo'
url: 'https://pypi.org/project/gonzalgo/'
abstract: >-
  Reports what a formal library rests on. A proof assistant can confirm that a
  proof checks; it cannot readily tell you that the theorem is standing on an
  unfinished proof several files upstream, or on trusting the compiler rather
  than the kernel. gonzalgo computes the declaration dependency graph, keeps
  statement dependencies separate from proof dependencies, and answers three
  questions no assistant answers directly: where an axiom is spent rather than
  inherited, which step introduced a given dependency, and whether any theorem
  reaches an unfinished proof or a compiler-trusting result. Supports Lean 4 and
  the Metamath databases set.mm, iset.mm, nf.mm, ql.mm and hol.mm, measured by
  one program so foundations are compared under identical definitions.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - Metamath
  - proof assistant
  - formal verification
  - axiom of choice
  - sorry
  - native_decide
  - dependency analysis
  - provenance
  - constructive mathematics
  - reverse mathematics
